---
/**
 * Accessibility statement. States an intent and a target (WCAG 2.2 AA) —
 * never a claim of certification or perfect compliance, and never an
 * accessibility-overlay product or automated-compliance badge.
 */

import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import siteConfig, { formatPageTitle } from "../data/siteConfig";

const title = formatPageTitle("Accessibility");
const description = `${siteConfig.bandNameFormal}'s commitment to making this website accessible.`;
const email = siteConfig.contact.email;
---

<LegalPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  kicker="Legal"
  heading="Accessibility Statement"
  effectiveDate="August 15, 2026"
>
  <p>
    The Electric Lavender Train is committed to making this website usable by as many people as
    possible, including people who use assistive technology such as screen readers, people who
    navigate by keyboard alone, and people with low vision or other disabilities.
  </p>

  <h2>Our target</h2>
  <p>
    We're working toward the <strong>Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2, Level AA</strong> as our design and development target. This is a goal we're actively working toward, not a
    certification — we do not claim this website is perfectly or completely compliant with WCAG or
    any other accessibility standard, and we do not use any accessibility-overlay product or
    automated tool that claims to make a website instantly or fully compliant. Real accessibility
    comes from how the site is actually built, tested, and maintained.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <p>Some of the practices reflected in how this website is built:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Semantic HTML, logical heading structure, and visible keyboard focus indicators throughout;</li>
    <li>Form fields with real, associated labels, and validation errors that are announced accessibly rather than communicated by color alone;</li>
    <li>Support for reduced-motion preferences — visitors who indicate a preference for less motion see substantially reduced animation across the site;</li>
    <li>Descriptive alternative text on meaningful images, and accessible titles on embedded video players;</li>
    <li>A layout designed to remain usable when zoomed or reflowed to a narrow viewport; and</li>
    <li>Interactive controls sized to meet WCAG 2.2's Target Size (Minimum) criterion — generally at least 24×24 CSS pixels, or equivalent spacing — with many primary controls (buttons, tabs, form fields) sized larger still as an internal usability goal.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reporting an accessibility barrier</h2>
  <p>
    Accessibility is an ongoing effort, not a one-time task — this website continues to be reviewed
    and improved over time. If you encounter a barrier using it, please tell us. Email
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> with a description of the issue and the page where you
    found it, and we'll do our best to address it.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
